RandomCurvesOverVerySmallFiniteFields -- randomly chosen smooth canonical curves over small finite fields
*********************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

This package can be seen as a refined version of the *note
RandomCanonicalCurves: (RandomCanonicalCurves)Top, package, which catches all
possible missteps in the constructions. The construction follows the
unirationality proof of M_g for g<=14 and the article Matrix factorizations and
families of curves of genus 15 (see http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.6962 ) for the
genus g=15 case. Since a unirational parametrization of M_g is only a rational
map, bad choices of parameters in the construction might end up in the
indeterminacy locus or other undesired subloci. Since for example a
hypersurface in characteristic 2 contains about 90% of the F_2-rational points
(see A quick and dirty irreducibility Test for Multivariate Polynomials over
F_q (see http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0404342 )), a failure of the construction in
the various steps is quite likely. We catch all possible missteps, and try
again until success.


For g<=10 we construct the canonical curves via plane models.


For 10<g<14 the canonical curves are constructed via space models.


For g=14 the construction is based on Verra's proof of the unirationality of
M_14 (see  The unirationality of the moduli space of curves of genus ≤14 (see
http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0402032 ) ).


The g=15 construction relies on matrix factorizations and is based on the
Macaulay2 Package Matrix factorizations and families of curves of genus 15 (see
http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.6962 ).


 For g <=14, the methods used in this package are based on the Macaulay2
Package *note RandomCurves: (RandomCurves)Top,  and the methods for the g=15
case are based on the Macaulay2-package MatFac15 (see
http://www.math.uni-sb.de/ag-schreyer/images/data/computeralgebra/M2/doc/
Macaulay2/MatFac15/html/index.html ).

