Details -- keeps track of the precise step in the construction of canonical genus 14 and 15 curves. Default value is "false".
*****************************************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

Setting the option Details to true displays the precise step in the
construction which is currently performed. This option displays additional
information compared to the option Printing. The purpose of this additional
option is to further test and tweak the genus 14 and 15 construction. The
output displayed uses the notation from the sourcecode. Thus, without having a
look into the sourcecode this option might not be helpful.

The default value for all functions is false.

Enabling this option also enable the option Printing.

See also
========

  * *note Printing: Printing, -- displays information about the current step in
    the constructions. Default value is "false".
  * *note smoothCanonicalCurve: smoothCanonicalCurve, -- Computes the ideal of
    canonical curve
  * *note smoothCanonicalCurveGenus14: smoothCanonicalCurveGenus14, -- Compute
    a random canonical curve of genus 14
  * *note smoothCanonicalCurveGenus15: smoothCanonicalCurveGenus15, -- Computes
    the ideal of canonical curve of genus 15

