isSmoothCurve -- Tests smoothness of a curve
********************************************

  * Usage: 
        isSmoothCurve(IC)
  * Inputs:
      * IC, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the Ideal of a curve
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, , whether the curve is
        smooth or not

Description
===========

Checks whether a curve is smooth or not



+-------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[x,y,z];            |
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : IC = ideal(x*y);          |
|                               |
|o2 : Ideal of S                |
+-------------------------------+
|i3 : isSmoothCurve(IC)         |
|                               |
|o3 = false                     |
+-------------------------------+
|i4 : IC2 = ideal (x^2+y^2+z^2);|
|                               |
|o4 : Ideal of S                |
+-------------------------------+
|i5 : isSmoothCurve(IC2)        |
|                               |
|o5 = true                      |
+-------------------------------+

